  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every route in this task and SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter. Fail closed. A missing caller oid, an unresolvable Dataverse user, an empty accessible business-unit set, a fault reading the config's business unit, a fault reading the business-unit hierarchy, or a fault reading the config table for the identity check DENIES. No path falls back to "allow" or to an unscoped query. An unknown config id and an out-of-scope config id get the identical answer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugins. Every check runs in the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9">Scope: the three /api/admin/record-matching routes. They are operator routes: require the existing "SystemAdmin" policy on the GROUP with `.RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin")`, exactly as `JobsEndpoints.cs:51-54` does, replacing the bare `.RequireAuthorization()` at `RecordMatchingAdminEndpoints.cs:14`. Do not create a new policy, do not add an endpoint filter for this, and do not modify the "SystemAdmin" policy at `AuthorizationModule.cs:362-377` (it is shared by /api/admin/jobs, /api/admin/membership and /api/ai/rag/admin). Do not add a per-record check: these routes take no record id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9">Scope: the /api/spe group. Do NOT add `.RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin")` to `SpeAdminEndpoints.cs` or to any /api/spe child group. Layer 1 (`SpeAdminAuthorizationFilter`) already requires the same two app roles, and the policy's empty 403 would replace the `sdap.access.deny.role_insufficient` ProblemDetails the client keys on (`speApiClient.ts:123-129`). Do not change `SpeAdminAuthorizationFilter`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the three record-matching 500 paths (`RecordMatchingAdminEndpoints.cs:68-71`, `:99-102`, `:122-125`). Replace `detail: ex.Message` with `ProblemDetailsHelper.Explain(&lt;the route's existing title&gt;, ex)`, the redacting helper ConfigEndpoints already uses. Keep status 500 and the existing titles. Leave `IndexSyncResult.Errors` and the 400 for a missing `since` (:84-87) unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Scope: the six /api/spe routes. The tenant-scope decision for a config the request NAMES stays in the ONE group filter, `SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter`. Do NOT add a per-handler `CanAccessConfigAsync` call to any route; the filter's own remarks (:36-41) explain why a per-endpoint check is the failure mode. The only in-handler checks allowed are on POST and PUT /api/spe/configs: the business-unit intersection and the app-identity check, because they judge BODY values that are not the config being acted on (a POST has no configId at all). This follows the `ListConfigsAsync` precedent (`ConfigEndpoints.cs:132-153`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: GET/PUT/DELETE /api/spe/configs/{id}. Rename the route parameter from `{id:guid}` to `{configId:guid}` (and the handler parameter to `configId`) so that the filter's route-value read applies. The URL shape does not change, so `speApiClient.ts:459-487` is unaffected. Do not add `id` as a key the filter reads (EnvironmentEndpoints uses `{id:guid}` for environment records, `EnvironmentEndpoints.cs:60`, `:86`, `:101`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter configId sources. The filter reads configId from ALL THREE places: the query key `configId`, the route value `configId`, and the bound body argument. For the body, endpoint filters run after parameter binding, so `EndpointFilterInvocationContext.Arguments` already holds the bound request record; do not buffer or re-read the request body. A slot counts as PRESENT when its raw value is non-empty, parseable or not. When two or more slots are present and they do not all parse to the same Guid, answer 400 ProblemDetails (title "Bad Request", `errorCode` "spe.admin.deny.config_id_ambiguous", `traceId`) BEFORE any Dataverse call — never authorize one value and let the handler act on another. When exactly one slot is present and it does not parse to a non-empty Guid, pass through unchanged so the handler's existing 400 answers (`BulkOperationEndpoints.cs:131-138`, `:185-192`). The client keeps sending configId in the body: do not move it to the query string and do not change `speApiClient.ts`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the uniform 404. Every "config not found" answer on the five filtered routes — the filter's out-of-scope 404, the filter's new does-not-exist 404, and the four ConfigEndpoints handler 404s that remain for a config deleted between the filter and the handler (`:219-223`, `:234-238`, `:381-385`, `:456-460`) — comes from ONE shared helper and is identical apart from the trace id value: status 404, title "Not Found", detail "Container type config '{configId}' was not found.", `errorCode` "spe.admin.deny.config_out_of_scope" (the existing value), and exactly the extension keys `errorCode` and `traceId` (the handlers' `correlationId` key is dropped on these four 404s only). No shipped client keys on that code (grep of src 2026-10-02: `speApiClient.ts:159` reads `errorCode`/`reasonCode` only to match three other codes).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: SpeAdminTenantScope / SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter fault handling. Replace the fail-open `return true` on a lookup fault (`SpeAdminTenantScope.cs:101-116`) with a deny that the filter can tell apart from "out of scope" (for example a small result type: permitted / not found or out of scope / unverifiable). The filter answers "unverifiable" with 503 ProblemDetails (title "Service Unavailable", `errorCode` "spe.admin.deny.scope_unverifiable", `traceId`), and the handler is not invoked. `GetAccessibleBusinessUnitsAsync` keeps THROWING on a hierarchy fault (`LoadBusinessUnitHierarchyAsync` :207-226 stays uncaught), so `ListConfigsAsync`'s existing catch keeps its 500; the filter and the POST/PUT checks catch that fault and answer the same 503. `ResolveCallerBusinessUnitAsync` (:141-178) keeps swallowing its own faults into an empty set (already fail-closed: the caller gets the uniform 404 on the filtered routes and the 403 on POST/PUT). Keep the class uncached (its remarks :33-39).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: POST /api/spe/configs and PUT /api/spe/configs/{configId}, business unit. Copy the intersection from `ListConfigsAsync` (`ConfigEndpoints.cs:132-153`). POST: a missing or `Guid.Empty` `businessUnitId` is a 400 validation error returned with the other field validations, before any Dataverse call. POST and PUT: a `businessUnitId` that is not in the caller's accessible set — whether it belongs to another unit or does not exist at all — gets ONE 403 via `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden("spe.admin.deny.business_unit_out_of_scope", ..., traceId)`, and `CreateAsync` / `UpdateAsync` is never called. An empty accessible set gets the same 403. Do not change the business-unit-less compatibility rule in `CanAccessConfigAsync` (escalation trigger 1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: POST /api/spe/configs and PUT /api/spe/configs/{configId}, app identity (finding #74). The five identity fields are `containerTypeId`, `owningAppId`, `keyVaultSecretName`, `consumingAppId`, `consumingAppKvSecret`. On POST, for every identity field supplied; on PUT, for every identity field whose trimmed value differs (case-insensitive) from the stored row the handler already reads (`UpdateConfigAsync` :371-372): refuse if ANY OTHER config row carries the same value (trimmed, case-insensitive) AND has a business unit outside the caller's accessible set. Rows with no business unit do not block (compatibility rule). Read the candidate rows with ONE app-only `QueryAsync` over `sprk_specontainertypeconfigs` selecting `sprk_specontainertypeconfigid`, `_sprk_businessunit_value` and the five columns, with NO caller value in the `$filter` (`DataverseWebApiClient.QueryAsync` does not URL-encode the filter, `:230`), and compare in memory, copying the `LoadBusinessUnitHierarchyAsync` shape (`top: 5000`). If the read faults, or returns 5000 rows (possible truncation), answer the 503 above. The refusal is ONE 403 via `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden("spe.admin.deny.config_identity_out_of_scope", ..., traceId)` whose detail does not name the other config or its business unit; `CreateAsync` / `UpdateAsync` is never called. Run the business-unit check first, then this one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: BulkOperationService per-item processing. Before soft-deleting or granting on a container, read it with the config's Graph client (`SpeAdminGraphService.GetContainerAsync`, :1281, which returns `ContainerTypeId` as a string) and act only if `Guid.TryParse` succeeds on both its `ContainerTypeId` and the resolved config's `ContainerTypeId` and the two Guids are equal. A container that is not found, a container of another type, an unparseable type id on either side, and a fault on the read all get the SAME per-item error text, count as Failed, and get no write. Put the per-item step (read, compare, then write or refuse) in one `internal` method per job kind that takes the `GraphServiceClient` and the resolved config as parameters, and have the job loop call it, so a test can drive it with the real Graph client from `GraphWireMockFixture` and a real `SpeAdminGraphService` built as `SpeAdminContainerArchivalContractTests.CreateSut` builds one. Do not modify `SpeAdminGraphService.cs`. Do not move the check to enqueue time (a 500-item synchronous Graph pass on the request thread), and do not add caller identity to the background job.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: "nothing is enqueued". `BulkOperationService` is sealed, so it cannot be mocked. Add one `internal` read-only property returning the number of tracked operations (`_statuses.Count`); the test assemblies already have InternalsVisibleTo (`Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj:43-51`). Tests assert it is unchanged after a refused request. No other new member on the service besides the two per-item methods.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Substitute at the `DataverseWebApiClient` class boundary (the DelegationRuleTestFixture pattern) and at `IDataverseIndexSyncService` (a recording fake registered after the real one, with `DocumentIntelligence:RecordMatchingEnabled=true` in the host configuration so the routes are mapped). Drive the real `Map*Endpoints` through a real host (WebApplicationFactory), as SpeAdminContainerItemRouteGateTests does: a test that calls the filter class directly does not prove the filter is attached. Graph calls go through the WireMock HTTP fake. No live Dataverse, Graph or AI Search in CI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: every new guard. Prove it bites by seeding: remove or revert the guard locally, run its test, confirm the named test FAILS, restore, and record each result in the task note (the practice at `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:517-518`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project hard gate">Scope: before the PR. Run the affected tests, the full BFF unit suite (`tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests`), NetArchTest (`tests/Spaarke.ArchTests`), and BOTH integration suites in full: `dotnet test tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests` AND `dotnet test tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests`. A build is not a run.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision (in BFF: these are existing BFF routes and an existing BFF filter; no new service, no new DI registration) citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Measure publish size against a FRESH build of origin/master from a short path, both sides zipped with Compress-Archive, file counts equal; report both absolute sizes and the delta; ceiling 60 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: no new HIGH. Run `/conflict-check` (sdap-SPE-admin-app-r3 is seeded against `SpeAdminGraphService.cs`; this task only reads it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: new surface. No new filter class, no new policy, no new service and no new DI registration. Extend `SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter` and `SpeAdminTenantScope`. Any new type (a scope-decision result type, a marker interface for body-carried configIds, the shared 404 helper) or new member carries the three-question justification in the PR with grep evidence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner (binding)">Scope: live Dataverse, Graph and AI Search. Read-only during development. Live writes are the main session's manual gate. No scope cuts; scope discovered during execution is added to this task and recorded in the note.</constraint>
