JUSTIFICATION (CLAUDE.md §11), new surface — full table with grep evidence in note §10.3: enum SpeAdminEnvironmentOperation (the filter must tell a by-id read from a write; cost: environments stay writable by leaf admins); WithSpeAdminEnvironmentScope on the existing extensions class (named wrapper over WithMetadata, the Compose endpoints' existing pattern); SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter.EnvironmentNotFound + two codes (cost: existence oracle, seed F4); record SpeAdminEnvironmentReach (one shared answer for list, filter and config write; cost: divergent copies); SpeAdminTenantScope.GetEnvironmentReachAsync (extends the existing boundary class); SpeAdminScopeDecision.EnvironmentOutOfScope (member of the existing enum; cost: any environment linkable); CanonicalIdentityValue / CanonicalIdentityColumnValue (cost: N/B/P GUID spellings bypass the identity check, seeds G1/G2); DashboardEndpoints.CompletenessConcern (cost: leaf admin sees the tenant-wide skipped-config count, seed D1).

TESTS (r1, justified one line each in note §10.4): SpeAdminEnvironmentScopeTests (38); non-canonical GUID tests (POST/PUT theories, stored-side, re-send twin); dashboard full-view + refresh tests (3); negative-twin route test; SystemAdmin admission rewrite; SearchItemsTests rewrite. r2 added no test. No ADR-038 banned pattern.

