    <outcome date="2026-10-04" branch="task/uac-r2-165-f1">
FOLLOW-UP ROUND f1 — OWNER ROUND 20 ITEMS 1-3, ROUND 25 ITEM 5, VERIFIER ITEMS 4-7: CODE-COMPLETE; ONLY MANUAL LIVE GATES REMAIN. Full record: notes/task-165-admin-surfaces.md §11 (§11.16 = the gates with exact commands).

BRANCH: task/uac-r2-165-f1 from task/uac-r2-165-r2 @ 87d098ba4. NOTE-FROM-MAIN.md read (binding) and not committed. Conflict-check clean (21 open PRs, none touches a changed path; merge-tree into work/unified-access-control-r2 @ 73296ce14 clean).

ROUND 20 ITEM 1 — DONE: every BFF container-creation path stamps the container's owning business unit as the fileStorageContainer custom property spaarkeBusinessUnitId (ONE owner: SpeContainerBusinessUnitStamp), reads it back, and removes the container if the stamp did not land. Admin plane POST /api/spe/containers: owner = the config's unit, else the creating admin's unit, else 403 spe.admin.deny.container_owner_unresolved; stamp failure 503 (removed) / 500 naming the container (removal failed), spe.containers.business_unit_stamp_failed. Secure-record provisioning: the Secure Record unit. The custom-property route refuses to set or change the stamp (403 spe.admin.deny.container_binding_server_owned); an unchanged re-send (the shipped editor's full-map save) is accepted and stripped. Backfill scripts/Backfill-SpeContainerBusinessUnitStamp.ps1 (dry run / -Apply / -Verify / -RevertManifest / -MaxWritesPerRun): owner derived only from businessunit.sprk_containerid, secure roots' sprk_containerid and CreateContainer audit rows (nearest common ancestor of claimants); underivable / mismatch / foreign / malformed LISTED, never written. Dev dry run (read-only): 5 containers, ToStamp 2, Underivable 3; -Verify now also fails on a config whose containers could not be listed (found by the dry run: config 68f9a952 stores the secret name "null"). -Apply NOT run (manual gate).
ROUND 20 ITEM 2 (+ verifier items 1, 3) — DONE: SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter decides PER CONTAINER after the configId rule, for the route value {containerId} or a body implementing the new ISpeAdminContainerScopedRequest: a container bound to the caller's own unit or a descendant; unbound or malformed only for a root-unit admin; unreadable binding 503; absent / other type / foreign = ONE 404 spe.admin.deny.container_out_of_scope, byte-identical to the handlers' not-found (shared helpers); route/body disagreement 400. 31 container routes (29 active + 2 recycle-bin, read from deletedContainers); ContainerItemEndpoints {id} renamed {containerId}. Lists and searches trimmed (503 on any binding fault; search totalCount withheld unless a platform operator saw nothing trimmed). Bulk: scope captured at enqueue (503 if unreadable), every item checked in the job (type reported and equal AND the per-container rule) before its Graph write; GET /bulk/{operationId}/status bound to its starter. App-only container-type routes (permissions GET; consumers GET/POST/PUT/DELETE; register) marked: type must be the config's (404 spe.admin.deny.container_type_out_of_scope), writes need every config of the type reachable (403 spe.admin.deny.container_type_shared).
ROUND 20 ITEM 3 — DONE: configs of different customers may share containerTypeId, owningAppId and keyVaultSecretName; only consumingAppId and consumingAppKvSecret stay exclusive (kind grouping across columns kept). Supersedes D5b.
ROUND 25 ITEM 5 (+ verifier item 2) — DONE: SpeDashboardSyncService is an IScheduledJob (spe-dashboard-sync) on ScheduledJobHost, AddScheduledJob with a cron from SpeAdmin:DashboardSyncIntervalMinutes (AddSingleton + AddHostedService, PeriodicTimer and refresh channel removed; WorkloadPlacementGuardTests baseline 13 -&gt; 12); refresh = TriggerNowAsync; first empty view starts a run. Each container attributed once to the config of its own unit or nearest ancestor (unit-less configs never receive bound containers; unbound = unattributed; unreadable binding = excluded + per-config concern). Metrics carry per-config storage and unattributed figures; a leaf admin sees its own storage (D4 retired); unattributed only in the platform operator's full view.
VERIFIER ITEMS 5 + 6 — DONE: GetReachableConfigIdsAsync full-page guard -&gt; SpeAdminDashboardScopeTests.WhenTheConfigReadMayBeTruncated_TheDashboardIs503_NeverTheTenantWideFigures (seed S24 RED); handler-side uniform 404 -&gt; SpeAdminConfigAndBulkTenantScopeTests.AConfigGoneBetweenTheFilterAndTheHandler_GetsTheFiltersExact404 (S25 RED) and the container twins (S26 RED).
VERIFIER ITEM 7 — DONE: SpeAdminConfigScopedBodyGuardTests scans every complex handler parameter in Api.SpeAdmin (records nested in endpoint classes) plus Models.SpeAdmin *Request; ConfigId needs ISpeAdminConfigScopedRequest, ContainerId needs ISpeAdminContainerScopedRequest; non-vacuity test (S13, S31 RED).
